<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Superfuse</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;1st May,&amp;nbsp;1982 / 06:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Location:&lt;/STRONG&gt; South Atlantic&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;6 Hours&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/STRONG&gt; United Kingdom&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Early on the morning of the 1st of May, a lone Vulcan bomber attacked Stanley airport; this was the longest-ranged recorded bombing mission in history. This was followed up by Sea Harriers from the RN task group striking Stanley airport again, with a further strike on Goose Green airfield.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Argentine forces were caught unaware by the Vulcan strike, but were expecting a follow up strike by Sea Harriers.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario has been enhanced with the "Fog of War" aspect - therefore expect the unexpected.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario Author: The Stig&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Historical Outcome (SPOILERS)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;After the Vulcan strike at Stanley airfield, Sea Harriers from Hermes with CAP support by from Invincible conducted strikes against Stanley airfield and Goose Green airstrip. Some damage was caused to the runway by the Vulcan's bombing run, followed by the Sea Harrier strikes on the airfield infrastructure. Only one Sea Harrier was hit by small arms fire .&lt;/EM&gt;</ScenDescription>
